      "width": 829,
      "height": 1269,
      "mime": "image/gif",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Desmarais and sons",
      "credit": "Photograph is Desmarais and sons; Actual photo was scanned from personal collection of family portraits",
      "source": "Charles-Gédéon Giasson & Agathe Macomber, full picture",
      "description": "Charles-Gédéon Giasson et Agathe McComber, de Kahnawake. Charles-Giasson and Agathe McComber married in 1832. They lived in Kahnawake and had many children including Léon-Trefflé Akiohanes Giasson and Napoléon-Antoine Giasson. The first married Agnès Brault in 1886 and the second married Marguerite Meunier dite Lafleur in 1875. Agathe McComber died in 1889 at the age of eighty-one. Interestingly, the attorney hired by the Giasson family to prevent their planned eviction in the late 1800s was Albert-Emmanuel de Lorimier, a son of controversial George de Lorimier (see other pictures). Albert-E. de Lorimier eventually obtained for the Giasson's their right to remain in Kahnawake.",
      "dateCreated": "19<sup>th</sup> century<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P,+1850-00-00T00:00:00Z/7</div>",
